    <div class="container">
      <h2>What Our Gas Safe Plumber Checks at Your Wirral Property</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We cover the boiler, gas cooker and hob, each inspected individually. The inspection takes 30 to 45 minutes for a single appliance.</p>
      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Gas supply pressure and flow rate</strong><p>Gas supply pressure tested at the meter and at each appliance. Low pressure or restricted flow can cause appliances to operate unsafely.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Gas leak check</strong><p>All pipework and appliance connections tested for gas leaks using calibrated detection equipment. Any leak classified under the Gas Industry Unsafe Situations Procedure.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Flue integrity and combustion products</strong><p>All flues tested for integrity, correct sealing and safe discharge. Open-flue appliances receive the combustion spillage testing they need.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Ventilation adequacy</strong><p>Each appliance we cover is checked for adequate ventilation. Blocked or inadequate ventilation is a common cause of incomplete combustion and carbon monoxide risk, particularly in older Birkenhead and Wallasey terraces.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Safety device operation</strong><p>All appliance safety devices tested individually. Each must demonstrate correct operation before the appliance can pass the inspection.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Signs of incomplete combustion</strong><p>Checked for staining, sooting or carbon deposits around appliances. Particularly important for open-flue appliances, where these signs are more common than on sealed combi boilers.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Boiler, gas cooker and hob</strong><p>Each one inspected individually and recorded separately on the CP12. We do not inspect gas fires or back boilers. Tell us about them when you book and we will explain your options.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>CP12 certificate issued and emailed same day</strong><p>Digital CP12 emailed the same day. Includes the engineer's Gas Safe registration number, inspection date and result for every appliance checked.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
