        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GAS FIRE</span>&nbsp; Does the CP12 need to cover the gas fire as well as the boiler?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. By law, the CP12 must cover every gas appliance the landlord supplies, including a gas fire. A certificate that covers only the boiler and not a landlord's gas fire is incomplete. Many older Wirral properties in CH41, CH42 and CH44 have gas fires. We cover boilers, gas cookers and hobs. We do not inspect gas fires or back boilers. Got a gas fire? Tell us when you book. If you no longer need it, we can disconnect and cap it safely, so it no longer has to be on the certificate. If you want to keep using it, it must be checked by an engineer registered for gas fires.</p></div></details>
